.TH DILOAD 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
diload \- load history entries in didump format into a history file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diload
[
.B \-f
]
[
.B \-u
]
[
.B \-h
.I hsize
]
[
.B \-v
]
[
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.I historyfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I diload
reads history entries in the format written by
.IR didump (8)
("DUMP \fIhash\fP.\fIiter\fP gm=... ex=... boff=... bsize=... flags=")
from standard input and adds them to
.IR historyfile ,
creating it if needed.  A line holding a single dot ends the input.
Entries already in the file are not added twice.  Together with didump
it is used to rebuild, move or resize a history file:
.PP
.nf
didump /news/dhistory | diload -h 8m /news/dhistory.new
.fi
.PP
At the end it prints how many entries were loaded out of how many read.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Fast mode: no locking and no duplicate checks.  Only for a new file;
an existing file is refused unless \fB\-u\fP is given too.
.TP
.B \-u
With \fB\-f\fP, allow an existing file and check for duplicates.  Not
recommended.
.TP
.BI \-h " hsize"
Hash table size (entries) for a new file, a power of 2, with an optional
k or m suffix.  Default: hsize in diablo.config.
.TP
.B \-v
Show progress.
.TP
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
Set the debug level.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
didump(8),
dhisexpire(8),
diloadfromspool(8),
diablo-files(5)
